.TH KEYHOLDTEST 1
.SH NAME
keyholdtest \- check keyhold(2)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keyholdtest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Keyholdtest
checks
.IR keyhold (2):
that a press sets its action and a release clears it, that a second key
bound to the same action works it too, that
.I edge
reports only what is new, and that a key outside the table changes
nothing rather than clearing what is held.
.PP
Two of its checks are about one trap, because it is the trap the module
exists for: a plain arrow key carries
.B Spec
and
.B Keyup
is
.BR Spec|0x800 ,
so a mask that tests only for the release bit reads a Left arrow
.I press
as a release.
A program that got it wrong would walk left for ever the moment an arrow
key was touched.
.PP
It needs no display.
The last line is
.B PASSED
or
.BR FAILED .
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
emu \-r. /dis/keyholdtest.dis
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/keyholdtest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR keyhold (2)
.SH BUGS
It drives
.I Binding.key
with key codes made up here rather than with codes a window actually
delivered, so it checks the decoding and not the plumbing.
That a window receives releases at all is
.IR keyuptest (1)'s
business.
